<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flint River (Georgia)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Flint River is a river of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, flowing south to join the Chattahoochee at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> border and form the Apalachicola. Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> towns lay along it in the 18th century, and the lands between it and the Ocmulgee were ceded under treaties of the early 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flint-river-georgia.jpg" alt="Flint River (Georgia)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Rivera · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oglethorpe_Ave_Bridge_over_Flint_River_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
